  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of a monoatomic gas is at a pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The density of the gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is the order of energy of the gas due to its thermal motion?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Internal energy is the energy due to thermal motion.</p><p>The internal energy of an ideal gas given by<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math> (for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>moles</mi></math>)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math> for&nbsp;a monoatomic gas.)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></math><br />So, the order of energy due to thermal motion is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p>"
  }
}